{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523978-m5-m1-setting-with-mtaw-system","id":1523978,"title":"M5: M1 setting with MtAw system?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-11T18:03:55-07:00","id":1523978,"title":"M5: M1 setting with MtAw system?","content":"Read MtA 1st edition corebook (only corebook, for settings changed a bit in M1 supplements\u2026 ) to get some impression<br /> <br /> In short it\u2019s basically a \u201cTechnocracy win\u201d world. They becomes the Biggest Worst Brother.<br /> <br /> Traditions are all purged into the Deep Umbra (I even think in M5 Traditions have failed the whole Ascension War, it\u2019s gone, for inspiration from W5\u2026 ).<br /> <br /> They CREATED the Gauntlet AND Autochthonia.<br /> <br /> They deploy space marines across the Earth to defend against so-called Outer Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now as a Tradition or Orphan mage you simply focus those minor victories\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> Fro systems maybe a mixture of MtA and MtAw (of course MtAw maybe more), although I used to have a far worse design (Traditions are completely broken, they fall into the pre-Tradition state and use Pillar/Foundation system in DAM\u2026 )<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T07:45:09-07:00","id":1524041,"title":"","content":"If I wanted a system more like Awakening, I\u2019d play Awakening, which would no doubt be the more superior version Awakening\u2019s mechanics. In the same manner that the touchstones in Requiem function a lot better than the touchstones of V5<br /> <br /> returning to pillars as a result of the technocracy winning does not actually make any sense on a metaphysical level, at the pillars worked because there was no consensus for paradox to arise from. Humanity\u2019s belief was still very much with the idea that magic is simply a fact of reality.<br /> <br /> Mechanically i think a lot would be lost from giving up on spheres entirely.<br /> <br /> The pillars are an attempt at allowing flexibility but only with a specific scope, they restrict what a mage can do so that it must fit within their fellowship\u2019s belief structures, but allow a lot of flexibility within said structures.<br /> <br /> The Arcana instead give everyone the same set of tools, and just make certain tools difficult to use for certain groups, and actually have all tools more or less do nothing useful or likely to do nothing at all unless you use reach.<br /> <br /> The spheres allow the greatest of freeform flexibility. While the arcana give you a nice long spell list to choose from, the spheres instead give a description of what sorts of things you can affect and how, letting you define for yourself the limits of your mage\u2019s capabilities. you also define your own limits by choosing a paradigm, practice, and instrument, and that defines which effects you can do, and what you need to do them.<br /> <br /> the focus of each is very different, and what I would prefer of a new edition is an attempt to better communicate how the spheres can be applied rather than to watch them be dismissed as an unworkable idea entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}